I'm trying to help someone who has been trying to adapt my scripts for 
use with a machine that has several aliased valid, routable IP addresses 
set up on his single NIC; he's apparently running a DNS on this box, 
with no "internal" network.  My script is set up for use with one IP on 
the external interface.  The script is working appropriately for the 
first IP on the list but is dropping everything destined for any of the 
others (as it should be).  Short of running a loop for each rule  
generated by the script that involves the external interface (which 
would be cumbersome but I know should work), does anyone else have (or 
could refer me to) a more efficient way of doing this?  I didn't find a 
way of doing it in Rusty's guides, but perhaps I should be looking 
somewhere besides the NAT docs?  

Thanks in advance -- Bob 
